\f0\fs24 \cf0 \expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Your profile reads less like a fixed \'93type\'94 and more like 
\f1\b a generally conscientious leader with some moderate pressure points around influence, recognition, reactivity, and interpersonal impact
\f0\b0 . The strongest protective features are your self-reported humility and ethical orientation; empathy is comparatively less developed but still in the emerging-capacity range.\
Importantly, these scores are 
\f1\b self-reported reflective indicators
\f0\b0 , not objective measurements of your character or behaviour. A moderate dark-signal score is best treated as a prompt to ask, \'93When might this tendency show up, and what safeguards help me manage it?\'94\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa298\partightenfactor0

\f1\b\fs36 \cf0 1. What the profile might suggest\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0

\fs28 \cf0 Overall leadership pattern\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f0\b0\fs24 \cf0 The combination of 
\f1\b Humility 82
\f0\b0  and 
\f1\b Ethical Leadership 79
\f0\b0  is encouraging. If those self-reports correspond reasonably well with your behaviour, you may already have useful internal safeguards: willingness to learn, capacity to acknowledge mistakes, concern for fairness, and an inclination to create trustworthy working relationships.\
Your 
\f1\b Empathy 64
\f0\b0  is an emerging capacity rather than a major weakness. This suggests an opportunity to become more deliberate about the 
\f2\i human impact
\f0\i0  of decisions rather than assuming good intentions automatically translate into good interpersonal outcomes.\
The four moderate reflective signals are worth viewing together:\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\ls1\ilvl0
\f1\b \cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Narcissism 46:
\f0\b0  You may be particularly worth watching for situations involving recognition, status, criticism, or perceived challenges to competence. The useful question isn't \'93Am I narcissistic?\'94 but 
\f1\b \'93What happens to my behaviour when I feel overlooked, criticised, or publicly contradicted?\'94
\f0\b0 \
\ls1\ilvl0
\f1\b \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Machiavellianism 57:
\f0\b0  This is your highest dark reflective signal. Under pressure, you may be tempted toward strategic communication\'97deciding carefully who gets which information, managing impressions, or treating influence primarily as an outcome to optimise. Your ethical-leadership score provides an important counterweight, so transparency can be an intentional safeguard.\
\ls1\ilvl0
\f1\b \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Psychopathy 39:
\f0\b0  This moderate signal may point to occasional impatience with emotional considerations, appetite for risk, bluntness, or insufficient consequence-checking\'97particularly when speed or results are heavily rewarded. It does 
\f1\b not
\f0\b0  establish reduced empathy or remorse as a personality fact.\
\ls1\ilvl0
\f1\b \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Sadism 43:
\f0\b0  The relevant behavioural watchpoint is not \'93cruelty,\'94 but what happens when you're angry, frustrated, or dealing with someone who has made a mistake. Humiliation, cutting humour, disproportionate punishment, or enjoying another person's setback would be useful warning signs to monitor.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0

\f1\b\fs28 \cf0 Likely context-sensitive triggers\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f0\b0\fs24 \cf0 These tendencies could become more salient when you are:\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\ls2\ilvl0\cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 under significant time pressure;\
\ls2\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 competing for recognition or influence;\
\ls2\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 receiving criticism in front of others;\
\ls2\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 dealing with someone you perceive as obstructive or incompetent;\
\ls2\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 holding substantially more organisational power than the other person;\
\ls2\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 incentivised to achieve a result at almost any cost;\
\ls2\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 angry after feeling disrespected or treated unfairly.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\cf0 Conversely, 
\f1\b clear ethical norms, trusted colleagues, meaningful dissent, adequate reflection time, and accountability
\f0\b0  may make these signals less consequential.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa298\partightenfactor0

\f1\b\fs36 \cf0 2. Three behavioural risks to monitor\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0

\fs28 \cf0 1. Strategic communication becoming too selective\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\fs24 \cf0 Watch for:
\f0\b0  withholding relevant context, tailoring information mainly to control an outcome, impression-managing rather than explaining your reasoning, or involving people only when their agreement is useful.\

\f1\b Safeguard:
\f0\b0  Ask, 
\f2\i \'93Who reasonably needs to know this to make a fair and informed decision?\'94
\f0\i0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0

\f1\b\fs28 \cf0 2. Reactivity when status, competence, or authority feels challenged\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\fs24 \cf0 Watch for:
\f0\b0  becoming unusually defensive, interrupting criticism, discounting a dissenting view, pushing to \'93win\'94 a disagreement, or making decisions while emotionally activated.\

\f1\b Safeguard:
\f0\b0  Build a deliberate pause between emotional activation and consequential action.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0

\f1\b\fs28 \cf0 3. Toughness becoming unnecessarily harsh\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\fs24 \cf0 Watch for:
\f0\b0  sarcasm at someone's expense, public correction when private correction would suffice, disproportionate consequences, dismissing emotional impact as irrelevant, or feeling unusually satisfied when someone who frustrated you experiences a setback.\

\f1\b Safeguard:
\f0\b0  Before acting, distinguish 
\f1\b accountability from humiliation
\f0\b0  and 
\f1\b firmness from retaliation
\f0\b0 .\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa298\partightenfactor0

\f1\b\fs36 \cf0 3. Three strengths/protective capacities\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0

\fs28 \cf0 1. Humility \'97 82\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f0\b0\fs24 \cf0 This is probably your most useful protective resource.\
Use it actively by:\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\ls3\ilvl0\cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 asking for dissent before decisions are final;\
\ls3\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 admitting uncertainty;\
\ls3\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 giving others visible credit;\
\ls3\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 correcting your own mistakes promptly.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\cf0 Humility can directly counter defensive responses to criticism and reduce the temptation to protect status or image.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0

\f1\b\fs28 \cf0 2. Ethical Leadership \'97 79\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f0\b0\fs24 \cf0 This provides a strong basis for managing the strategic-influence signal.\
Make transparency operational rather than merely aspirational: explain decision criteria, share relevant information fairly, maintain confidentiality appropriately, and make it safe for people to challenge you.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0

\f1\b\fs28 \cf0 3. Emerging Empathy \'97 64\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f0\b0\fs24 \cf0 Rather than treating 64 as a deficiency, treat it as a 
\f1\b trainable regulation mechanism
\f0\b0 .\
Perspective-taking can slow impulsive decisions and make consequences more visible. A simple question\'97
\f2\i \'93What is this likely to feel like from their position?\'94
\f0\i0 \'97can sometimes change the quality of a decision substantially.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa321\partightenfactor0

\f1\b\fs48 \cf0 4. A four-week improvement plan\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0

\fs28 \cf0 Week 1 \'97 Feedback tolerance\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\fs24 \cf0 Micro-experiment:
\f0\b0  Ask two trusted colleagues for one piece of behavioural feedback:\
\'93What's one thing I do as a leader that makes it easier to work with me, and one thing that occasionally makes it harder?\'94\
Your only job initially is to understand, not defend.\

\f1\b Observable behaviour:
\f0\b0  Don't explain or rebut the feedback during the first conversation. Ask one clarifying question and thank them.\

\f1\b Reflection:
\f0\b0 \
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\ls4\ilvl0\cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 What feedback did I instinctively want to reject?\
\ls4\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 What did I learn despite that reaction?\
\ls4\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Did I listen differently depending on who gave me the feedback?\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0

\f1\b\fs28 \cf0 Week 2 \'97 Transparent influence\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\fs24 \cf0 Micro-experiment:
\f0\b0  Before one consequential decision, explicitly share the decision criteria and relevant context with affected colleagues.\

\f1\b Observable behaviour:
\f0\b0  Document 
\f2\i why
\f0\i0  the decision is being made, what information was considered, and where genuine uncertainty remains.\

\f1\b Reflection:
\f0\b0 \
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\ls5\ilvl0\cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Did I share information people reasonably needed?\
\ls5\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Was I trying to persuade, or genuinely inform?\
\ls5\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Did anyone have a meaningful opportunity to disagree?\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0

\f1\b\fs28 \cf0 Week 3 \'97 Empathy and consequence-checking\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\fs24 \cf0 Micro-experiment:
\f0\b0  Before three non-trivial decisions, take a 60-second pause.\
Ask:\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\ls6\ilvl0\cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	1	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Who is affected?\
\ls6\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	2	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 What might they experience as a result?\
\ls6\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	3	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 What unintended consequence is easiest for me to overlook?\
\ls6\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	4	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Is there a less harmful way to achieve substantially the same objective?\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f1\b \cf0 Observable behaviour:
\f0\b0  Delay at least one non-urgent decision when you notice yourself becoming angry, rushed, or personally invested.\

\f1\b Reflection:
\f0\b0 \
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\ls7\ilvl0\cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Did the pause change my decision?\
\ls7\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Whose perspective was easiest to overlook?\
\ls7\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Did urgency actually require immediate action?\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0

\f1\b\fs28 \cf0 Week 4 \'97 Repair and reinforcement\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\fs24 \cf0 Micro-experiment:
\f0\b0  Identify one interaction where your impact may not have matched your intention.\
If appropriate, repair it without making the other person responsible for reassuring you.\

\f1\b Observable behaviour:
\f0\b0  Give specific credit to at least two colleagues, especially where their contribution might otherwise be invisible.\

\f1\b Reflection:
\f0\b0 \
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\ls8\ilvl0\cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Where did I handle pressure well?\
\ls8\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Where did I become more controlling, defensive, blunt, or dismissive?\
\ls8\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Which safeguard should become a permanent habit?\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\cf0 At the end of four weeks, look for 
\f1\b behavioural evidence
\f0\b0 , not a new \'93score\'94: fewer defensive reactions, clearer information-sharing, more dissent, better repairs, and fewer interactions you later wish you had handled differently.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa321\partightenfactor0

\f1\b\fs48 \cf0 5. Useful scripts\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0

\fs28 \cf0 Seeking feedback\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f0\b0\fs24 \cf0 \'93I'm working on becoming more effective under pressure. What's one behaviour of mine that you think I should keep, and one that I should change?\'94\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0

\f1\b\fs28 \cf0 Pausing before a reactive decision\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f0\b0\fs24 \cf0 \'93I want to make a good decision rather than a fast reaction. I'm going to take a little time to consider the consequences and come back to this.\'94\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0

\f1\b\fs28 \cf0 Giving credit\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f0\b0\fs24 \cf0 \'93I want to make sure the contribution is visible: [Name] did the key work on [specific contribution], and that materially improved the outcome.\'94\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0

\f1\b\fs28 \cf0 Repairing harm\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f0\b0\fs24 \cf0 \'93I don't think my intention excuses the impact. I was too [blunt/dismissive/etc.]. I'm sorry. I'll handle that differently next time.\'94\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0

\f1\b\fs28 \cf0 Responding ethically to conflict\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f0\b0\fs24 \cf0 \'93Let's separate the disagreement from the person. I want to understand your concern, make the decision criteria explicit, and address the issue without making this personal.\'94\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0

\f1\b\fs28 \cf0 When someone challenges you\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f0\b0\fs24 \cf0 \'93That's a useful challenge. Before I respond, let me make sure I understand what you're seeing that I may be missing.\'94\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa321\partightenfactor0

\f1\b\fs48 \cf0 6. Questions to ask before applying any suggestion\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f0\b0\fs24 \cf0 Context matters enormously. Before changing your behaviour, consider:\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\ls9\ilvl0
\f1\b \cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Power:
\f0\b0  Do I have substantially more authority than the other person?\
\ls9\ilvl0
\f1\b \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Safety:
\f0\b0  Could this conversation expose them to retaliation or disadvantage?\
\ls9\ilvl0
\f1\b \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Confidentiality:
\f0\b0  Am I entitled to share this information?\
\ls9\ilvl0
\f1\b \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Fairness:
\f0\b0  Would I apply the same standard if the roles were reversed?\
\ls9\ilvl0
\f1\b \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Proportionality:
\f0\b0  Is my response proportionate to the actual problem?\
\ls9\ilvl0
